---
title: "committee_reconfiguration (Sui Whitepaper: Epoch Transition)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_vote_end: quorum of stake for epoch e votes to end epoch
    q_vote_end --> q_checkpoint: authorities exchange info for end-of-epoch checkpoint
    q_checkpoint --> q_run_agreement: run agreement protocol for certified checkpoint
    q_run_agreement --> q_certify_checkpoint: checkpoint contains union of all processed transactions

    q_certify_checkpoint --> q_determine_committee: read stake delegation from checkpoint state
    q_determine_committee --> q_sign_new: new committee C_e_prime determined

    q_sign_new --> q_old_signs: quorum of old authorities signs new committee
    q_old_signs --> q_new_signs: quorum of new authorities signs new committee
    q_new_signs --> q_activate: both signature sets available

    q_activate --> q_start_new_epoch: new authorities start processing transactions for epoch e+1
    q_start_new_epoch --> q_cleanup: old authorities may delete epoch signing keys
    q_cleanup --> [*]: reconfiguration complete

    note right of q_certify_checkpoint
        INV-001: If Tx committed at epoch e or before, no conflicting Tx can be committed after e
        INV-002: If Tx committed at or before e, it must also be committed after e (liveness)
        INV-003: At least one honest authority includes each committed Tx in checkpoint
        INV-004: Locked owned objects recover at epoch boundary (equivocation recovery)
    end note
